Avengers end game co-director Joe Russo  has a few choice words for Oscar voters  critics are near unanimous in their  praise of the film and Robert Downey jr.  performance as Tony Stark  but if Russo were to have his way the  Marvel Cinematic Universe says biggest  star will take home an Academy Award for  the flick  according to the Washington Post heads  ur for some spoilers for Avengers  endgame ahead during a stop in a  nation's capital on a promotional tour  for the film late last week Russo didn't  hold back about the contributions a star  made not only to endgame but to the  Marvel Cinematic Universe and popular  culture in general he explained his  cumulative body of work from these  movies is staggering if you look at the  work over just even the last four Marvel  films he's done is phenomenal he  deserves an Oscar perhaps more than  anyone in the last 40 years because of  the way that he has motivated popular  culture there have been a lot of great  film performances in the last 40 years  and Russo's making quite a bold  statement but he does have a point  Downey kicked off the entire MCU with  what was seen at the time as an  improbably brilliant performance in 2008  sigh oh man and since then he has added  layers of depth and complexity to a  character that could have been more  OneNote in the hands of a lesser actor  according to cinema blend his casting  was seen by industry analysts as a  gamble when it was announced in 2007 I  am Iron Man  in the decade leading up to his first  triumphant Turner stark Dalia struggled  heavily with alcohol abuse a poor public  image and a tendency to confuse and  alienate those around him all issues  which had plagued stark for years and  the pages of Marvel Comics now Russo and  his co-director brother Anthony Russo  believed Downey's work should be taken  into consideration by the Academy's  voters Anthony said he has a very  involved process a more involved process  in any actor we've ever worked with he  digs deeper and he works harder than  anybody Downey really just goes the  extra mile for everything it's like  everything he's doing is something to  his core Joe Russo also made the points  that the Academy seems to have an  inherent bias against popular movies in  the modern era compared to past Oscar  Best Picture winners like The Sound of  Music The Godfather and rocky to name  just a few  he added we're talking about some of the  most popular films ever made it feels  like there's now a prejudice against  popular cinema in a way that's somewhat  sad Downey has been nominated for Oscars  twice before once for the title role in  the 1992 biopic Chaplin and again for  his controversial comedic turn in 2008  strop ik Thunder but he permeates at the  role of Tony Stark with his own  personality and with Ben's game he  masterfully brought a close to an arc  that has taken over 10 years to complete  part of the journey yet  it seems almost inconceivable now but  when Marvel Studios chose to lead off  their Cinematic Universe with Iron Man  the character was so obscure that the  choice left industry analysts scratching  their heads in the lead-up to its  release Marvel even commissioned short  animated films intended to raise the  characters public profile today the  character is become a household name one  of the most popular in all of mainstream  cinema and it almost certainly would  never have happened if Downey had not  poured his heart and soul into the  character every time he stepped in front  of the cameras for Marvel over the last  decade Plus Downey has delivered an  acting performance unlike any in film  history and for that we agree that he  deserves his industry's highest honor  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more loop of videos about  endgame and the MCU are coming soon  subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Applause]  [Music]
 

